Patch: 013-recovery-note-system-prompt
Reason: after a crash, the harness's account of the cut-off turn goes in the resuming drive's system prompt, sent fresh for that drive (snapshot off), and holds only the harness's own words: each call by name, id and status, never its input, output or error text; the resuming user turn holds only the user's own words (the prompts the transcript never got, then the messages sent since), or a bare "Continue."
Upstream: ours
Pins: after a crash mid-turn, the recovery note is in the resuming drive's system prompt (sent, not the recorded one) and in no user message; the user turn is a bare nudge
Pins: a tool output that reads as instructions reaches no system prompt and no user message after a crash: only the statuses do
